    "result_text": "All tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented per-country national-number length validation for E.164 telephones in `TelephoneE164.java`.\n\n**The change** (`src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/TelephoneE164.java`): after the existing normalization and the general 8\u201315 digit check, `toE164` now checks the national-number length against the country code:\n\n- `+61` (Australia) \u2192 requires exactly **9** national digits\n- `+1` (NANP) \u2192 requires exactly **10** national digits\n\nA number whose national digit count is wrong for its country throws `InvalidTelephoneException`, which the existing `InvalidTelephoneExceptionHandler` maps to **400 Bad Request**. Numbers with an unrecognized country code fall through to the general 8\u201315 rule as before.\n\nThe two known prefixes (`61`, `1`) are mutually exclusive (an Australian number starts with `6`, not `1`), so the map iteration order is safe. The `uniqueTelephone()` fixture (`04XXXXXXXX` \u2192 `+61` + 9 national digits) still passes the new rule, keeping the existing valid-owner flow green, and the new test `errorRejectsWrongNationalLength` (`\"+61 123\"`) is rejected with 400.",
